# cluster/inventory.env — single source of truth for the clio/urania cluster.
# Sourced by clusterctl (on ceres) and by the bootstrap scripts (on the nodes).
# Discovered 2026-06-17 by direct inspection of both hosts.

# ---- Control plane (how ceres reaches the nodes) ----
# Real DNS since cgk-dns-sync went live (UniFi clients -> cgk.sh at DNSimple); the bare mDNS names
# `clio`/`urania` no longer resolve from ceres, so use the FQDNs.
# Both nodes are wired at 10Gbase-T into the USW Flex XG (the old notes about urania being on WiFi
# at .39 and clio at 1GbE are obsolete — verified 2026-08-07).
CLIO_MGMT=clio.cgk.sh          # 10.10.10.149  (enP7s7, 10Gbase-T)
URANIA_MGMT=urania.cgk.sh      # 10.10.10.155  (enP7s7, 10Gbase-T; wlP9s9 is down)
SSH_USER=colby
CLUSTER_DOMAIN=cgk.sh   # nodes are <name>.$CLUSTER_DOMAIN; also the CN space for the private CA
SSH_KEY="/Users/colby/Library/Application Support/NVIDIA/Sync/config/nvsync.key"

# ---- High-speed fabric (clio <-> urania only; NOT reachable from ceres) ----
# 4x ConnectX-7 ports per host, each linked at 200 Gb/s (RoCE / Ethernet link layer).
# Two links are pre-configured and verified (ping ~0.9ms). Two are cabled (carrier up)
# but unconfigured; bootstrap will bring them up. Final assignment confirmed in 10-network.sh.
#
#   subnet         iface(both hosts)   clio          urania        status
#   10.51.50.0/24  enp1s0f1np1         10.51.50.13   10.51.50.12   configured (verified)
#   10.51.51.0/24  enP2p1s0f1np1       10.51.51.13   10.51.51.12   configured (verified)
#   10.51.52.0/24  enp1s0f0np0         10.51.52.13   10.51.52.12   TO CONFIGURE (link up)
#   10.51.53.0/24  enP2p1s0f0np0       10.51.53.13   10.51.53.12   TO CONFIGURE (link up)
#
# Primary fabric IPs used for inter-node service comms (Ray/NCCL bootstrap address):
CLIO_FABRIC=10.51.50.13
URANIA_FABRIC=10.51.50.12

# Mellanox RDMA devices (from ibstat): mlx5_0..mlx5_3 map to the 4 ports above.
RDMA_HCAS="mlx5_0,mlx5_1,mlx5_2,mlx5_3"
FABRIC_IFACES="enp1s0f1np1 enP2p1s0f1np1 enp1s0f0np0 enP2p1s0f0np0"
FABRIC_MTU=9000

# ---- Management LAN ----
# ceres (10.10.10.123), clio (.149) and urania (.155) all hang off one USW Flex XG at 10Gbase-T,
# so traffic between them never leaves that switch. LAN_MTU is what every host on it should agree
# on, and it must not exceed what the switch forwards: UniFi ships with Jumbo Frames DISABLED, and
# an oversized host MTU on a 1500 switch silently black-holes large packets (no ICMP comes back
# from an L2 switch, so path-MTU discovery never engages).
# To raise it: enable Jumbo Frames in the UniFi controller FIRST, then `clusterctl lan-mtu 9000`,
# then set ceres's en0 to match. Change this value only once the switch really carries it.
LAN_GATEWAY=10.10.10.1
LAN_MTU=9000            # jumbo enabled on the USW Flex XG 2026-08-07; all three hosts verified at 9000

# ---- Service ports ----
GATEWAY_PORT=4000       # LiteLLM Anthropic/OpenAI gateway (what Claude Code on ceres targets)
VLLM_PORT=8000          # per-node vLLM OpenAI server
COMFYUI_PORT=8188       # per-node ComfyUI, studio profile (nginx :443)
COMFYUI_PRIVATE_PORT=8189  # private profile (nginx :8443); also in cluster/comfyui/private.yaml
RAY_PORT=6379           # Ray head (for scale-up sharded mode)

# ---- Shared ComfyUI model store ----
# One copy of the models/ and input/ trees lives on COMFY_STORE_HOST and is NFSv4.2-over-RDMA
# exported to the other node across the fabric. Measured 1.5-1.8 GB/s vs ~970 MB/s for TCP
# nconnect=16. Set up by scripts/bootstrap/35-comfyui-share.sh; see docs/comfyui-shared-store.md.
COMFY_STORE_HOST=urania
COMFY_STORE_SERVER_IP=$URANIA_FABRIC     # exporter
COMFY_STORE_CLIENT_IP=$CLIO_FABRIC       # mounter (the only host allowed in /etc/exports)
COMFY_STORE_RDMA_PORT=20049

# ---- Head node (runs the gateway + Ray head in sharded mode) ----
# Used both as an ssh target and as the gateway hostname baked into ~/.clio/claude-code.env,
# so it needs to be the resolvable FQDN.
HEAD=clio.cgk.sh

# ---- Hardware facts (both nodes identical) ----
# GB10 Grace Blackwell, sm_121, 20-core ARM, ~119 GiB usable unified memory,
# 3.7 TB NVMe, driver 580.159.03 / CUDA 13.0, Ubuntu 24.04, kernel 6.17-nvidia.
# Docker 29.2.1 + nvidia-container-toolkit 1.19.1. MLNX OFED/DOCA 25.10, CX-7 fw 28.47.
NODE_UNIFIED_MEM_GIB=119
NODE_BW_GBPS=273        # LPDDR5X bandwidth ceiling — the real limiter on decode tok/s
